{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfA1CohXcte8f6G4Vbgv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012RStXLvgwak2hnHDv8TkUL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/mm-ref/eng/dist/handoff && sed -n 297,305p AI_GUIDE.md | cut -c1-1500; grep -n \"steps:\" my-3d2dge.js | head -12; grep -n \"drums\" my-3d2dge.js | head -8"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3404,"cache_read_input_tokens":123344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3404,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93b63dd9-a1ff-4df8-b77f-2b0e19e5047c","uuid":"2a97f907-a483-42db-b65a-f05989d58653","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:50:53.651Z","request_id":"req_011CgfA1CR8FtnYpCe4WMyYg","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012RStXLvgwak2hnHDv8TkUL":{"command":"cd /tmp/mm-ref/eng/dist/handoff && sed -n 297,305p AI_GUIDE.md | cut -c1-1500; grep -n \"steps:\" my-3d2dge.js | head -12; grep -n \"drums\" my-3d2dge.js | head -8"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012RStXLvgwak2hnHDv8TkUL","type":"tool_result","content":"### Audio\n- Browsers start sound only after the first key press or click; the engine waits for it.\n- `sfx(name)` ignores the same sound fired twice in 35 ms, and varies the pitch slightly so repeats don't sound robotic.\n- `music(song)` loops tracks of its own step notation. Every track loops on its own length, so short drum or bass loops can run under long melodies.\n- Built-in songs: `title`, `adventure`, `dungeon`, `boss`, `victory` (plays once). The songs module's songbook has more by mood (`E.Songbook.find('town')`) and jingles.\n- The music clock (the full engine): a song's place is game time (`audio.pos`), not the sound's, so beats land on the same update step headless and on any device, and the sound is held to that clock (it moves its notes to meet it). Time gameplay to `audio.pos`, `audio.at(step, fn)` and `audio.onBeat(fn)`, never to the sound. A song with `sync: true` pauses with the game.\n- Dynamic music: one song in layers rather than cuts. Name the tracks, start the extra ones with `on: false`, and bring them in with `audio.layer('drums', 1, .5)` (the stealth slice's chase); `audio.tempo(bpm)` for a hurry-up; `audio.sting(song, { at: 'bar' })` for a jingle on the next bar; `music(song, { fade: 1 })` to crossfade.\n\n### Text and UI\n29: *    update runs in exact fixed steps: each 1/120 s of real time is one update with\n2371:     *  updateMs, renderMs: milliseconds the last frame spent updating and drawing; steps: the updates it ran; items:\n2373:    this.stats = { updateMs: 0, renderMs: 0, frameMs: 16.7, steps: 0, items: 0, actors: 0, culled: 0 };\n2671:   * - boot: { title, version, steps: [[label, fn]], messages, min, checks, accent } runs the boot first (section 10c): the\n3153: *        steps: [['Raising the harbour', () => { map = buildHarbour(); }], ['Teaching the guards to look up', loadGuards]],\n7629:   * Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [\n7665:  // the clock now between the game's steps: what it read at the last frame and the real time since (to schedule the\n7713:    this.music({ bpm: 100, steps: 1, tracks: [{ wave: 'square', vol: .24, notes: 'C6 G5 G5 G5' }] }, { restart: true });\n7801:  title: { bpm: 112, steps: 4, tracks: [\n7805:  adventure: { bpm: 138, steps: 4, tracks: [\n7810:  dungeon: { bpm: 96, steps: 4, tracks: [\n7814:  boss: { bpm: 164, steps: 4, tracks: [\n7521:/* drum kit for music tracks with wave 'drums': k kick, s snare, h hat, o open hat, c crash, t tom */\n7632:   *   { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] }\n7689:  /** a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when\n7789:    if (t.wave === 'drums' || t.wave === 'noise') {\n7804:    { wave: 'drums', vol: .14, notes: 'k . h . s . h . k . h k s . h .' } ] },\n7809:    { wave: 'drums', vol: .15, notes: 'k . h . s . h h k . h . s . h o' } ] },\n7813:    { wave: 'drums', vol: .1, notes: 'k . . . h . . . k . k . h . . .' } ] },\n7818:    { wave: 'drums', vol: .16, notes: 'k h s h k k s h k h s h k s s s' } ] },\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-184717__xe8b2f0/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93b63dd9-a1ff-4df8-b77f-2b0e19e5047c","uuid":"1b88f9bf-81e4-4949-a414-96af7a1476c2","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:50:53.680Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### Audio\n- Browsers start sound only after the first key press or click; the engine waits for it.\n- `sfx(name)` ignores the same sound fired twice in 35 ms, and varies the pitch slightly so repeats don't sound robotic.\n- `music(song)` loops tracks of its own step notation. Every track loops on its own length, so short drum or bass loops can run under long melodies.\n- Built-in songs: `title`, `adventure`, `dungeon`, `boss`, `victory` (plays once). The songs module's songbook has more by mood (`E.Songbook.find('town')`) and jingles.\n- The music clock (the full engine): a song's place is game time (`audio.pos`), not the sound's, so beats land on the same update step headless and on any device, and the sound is held to that clock (it moves its notes to meet it). Time gameplay to `audio.pos`, `audio.at(step, fn)` and `audio.onBeat(fn)`, never to the sound. A song with `sync: true` pauses with the game.\n- Dynamic music: one song in layers rather than cuts. Name the tracks, start the extra ones with `on: false`, and bring them in with `audio.layer('drums', 1, .5)` (the stealth slice's chase); `audio.tempo(bpm)` for a hurry-up; `audio.sting(song, { at: 'bar' })` for a jingle on the next bar; `music(song, { fade: 1 })` to crossfade.\n\n### Text and UI\n29: *    update runs in exact fixed steps: each 1/120 s of real time is one update with\n2371:     *  updateMs, renderMs: milliseconds the last frame spent updating and drawing; steps: the updates it ran; items:\n2373:    this.stats = { updateMs: 0, renderMs: 0, frameMs: 16.7, steps: 0, items: 0, actors: 0, culled: 0 };\n2671:   * - boot: { title, version, steps: [[label, fn]], messages, min, checks, accent } runs the boot first (section 10c): the\n3153: *        steps: [['Raising the harbour', () => { map = buildHarbour(); }], ['Teaching the guards to look up', loadGuards]],\n7629:   * Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [\n7665:  // the clock now between the game's steps: what it read at the last frame and the real time since (to schedule the\n7713:    this.music({ bpm: 100, steps: 1, tracks: [{ wave: 'square', vol: .24, notes: 'C6 G5 G5 G5' }] }, { restart: true });\n7801:  title: { bpm: 112, steps: 4, tracks: [\n7805:  adventure: { bpm: 138, steps: 4, tracks: [\n7810:  dungeon: { bpm: 96, steps: 4, tracks: [\n7814:  boss: { bpm: 164, steps: 4, tracks: [\n7521:/* drum kit for music tracks with wave 'drums': k kick, s snare, h hat, o open hat, c crash, t tom */\n7632:   *   { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] }\n7689:  /** a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when\n7789:    if (t.wave === 'drums' || t.wave === 'noise') {\n7804:    { wave: 'drums', vol: .14, notes: 'k . h . s . h . k . h k s . h .' } ] },\n7809:    { wave: 'drums', vol: .15, notes: 'k . h . s . h h k . h . s . h o' } ] },\n7813:    { wave: 'drums', vol: .1, notes: 'k . . . h . . . k . k . h . . .' } ] },\n7818:    { wave: 'drums', vol: .16, notes: 'k h s h k k s h k h s h k s s s' } ] },","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-184717__xe8b2f0/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012RStXLvgwak2hnHDv8TkUL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfA2ps9R8xrFXa9YJKCe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019ycTDDGLRNkVgmJTnUg3XT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/mm-ref/eng/dist/handoff && sed -n 7626,7640p my-3d2dge.js | cut -c1-300; sed -n 7798,7806p my-3d2dge.js | cut -c1-400"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4072,"cache_read_input_tokens":126748,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4072,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93b63dd9-a1ff-4df8-b77f-2b0e19e5047c","uuid":"cd9f0646-d580-4aa1-9e1c-bb2becfa7c9c","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:50:55.227Z","request_id":"req_011CgfA2pVaJDyuAMeyDSX9o","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019ycTDDGLRNkVgmJTnUg3XT":{"command":"cd /tmp/mm-ref/eng/dist/handoff && sed -n 7626,7640p my-3d2dge.js | cut -c1-300; sed -n 7798,7806p my-3d2dge.js | cut -c1-400"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019ycTDDGLRNkVgmJTnUg3XT","type":"tool_result","content":"  /** add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 }) */\n  define(name, voice) { this.presets[name] = voice; }\n  /**\n   * Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [\n   *   { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' },   one token per step\n   *   { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' },\n   *   { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] }\n   * tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines).\n   * steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (len: steps, else\n   * its longest track's); a track may have a name, and on: false starts it silent (a layer that audio.layer brings in).\n   * THE MUSIC CLOCK: a song starts at the game's time and where it is is game time (audio.pos, headless too: the same\n   * steps hear the same beats); the sound follows that clock. o: { loop, sync: true (it pauses with the game, on\n   * game.time; else it plays on through a pause, on game.real), fade: seconds (a crossfade from the song playing),\n   * restart: true (again from its start, though it is the one playing) }.\n   * E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\n}\n/** ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions): title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory. game.audio.music('adventure') */\nE.songs = {\n  title: { bpm: 112, steps: 4, tracks: [\n    { wave: 'square', vol: .16, notes: 'C5 - - - G4 - C5 - E5 - - - D5 - C5 - | D5 - - - G4 - B4 - D5 - - - F5 - E5 - | E5 - - - C5 - E5 - G5 - - - A5 - G5 - | F5 - E5 - D5 - B4 - C5 - - - - - . .' },\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes: 'C3 - . C3 G2 - . G2 C3 - . C3 G2 - . G2 | G2 - . G2 D3 - . D3 G2 - . G2 D3 - . D3 | A2 - . A2 E3 - . E3 A2 - . A2 E3 - . E3 | F2 - . F2 G2 - . G2 C3 - . C3 G2 - . .' },\n    { wave: 'drums', vol: .14, notes: 'k . h . s . h . k . h k s . h .' } ] },\n  adventure: { bpm: 138, steps: 4, tracks: [\n    { wave: 'pulse', vol: .15, notes: 'E5 - G5 - A5 - - C6 B5 - A5 - G5 - E5 - | D5 - E5 - G5 - - A5 G5 - E5 - D5 - . . | E5 - G5 - A5 - - C6 D6 - C6 - A5 - G5 - | A5 - G5 - E5 - D5 - C5 - - - - - . .' },\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-184717__xe8b2f0/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93b63dd9-a1ff-4df8-b77f-2b0e19e5047c","uuid":"6387a727-e08c-465c-9d66-30d15d3da4de","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:50:55.249Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"  /** add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 }) */\n  define(name, voice) { this.presets[name] = voice; }\n  /**\n   * Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [\n   *   { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' },   one token per step\n   *   { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' },\n   *   { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] }\n   * tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines).\n   * steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (len: steps, else\n   * its longest track's); a track may have a name, and on: false starts it silent (a layer that audio.layer brings in).\n   * THE MUSIC CLOCK: a song starts at the game's time and where it is is game time (audio.pos, headless too: the same\n   * steps hear the same beats); the sound follows that clock. o: { loop, sync: true (it pauses with the game, on\n   * game.time; else it plays on through a pause, on game.real), fade: seconds (a crossfade from the song playing),\n   * restart: true (again from its start, though it is the one playing) }.\n   * E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\n}\n/** ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions): title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory. game.audio.music('adventure') */\nE.songs = {\n  title: { bpm: 112, steps: 4, tracks: [\n    { wave: 'square', vol: .16, notes: 'C5 - - - G4 - C5 - E5 - - - D5 - C5 - | D5 - - - G4 - B4 - D5 - - - F5 - E5 - | E5 - - - C5 - E5 - G5 - - - A5 - G5 - | F5 - E5 - D5 - B4 - C5 - - - - - . .' },\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes: 'C3 - . C3 G2 - . G2 C3 - . C3 G2 - . G2 | G2 - . G2 D3 - . D3 G2 - . G2 D3 - . D3 | A2 - . A2 E3 - . E3 A2 - . A2 E3 - . E3 | F2 - . F2 G2 - . G2 C3 - . C3 G2 - . .' },\n    { wave: 'drums', vol: .14, notes: 'k . h . s . h . k . h k s . h .' } ] },\n  adventure: { bpm: 138, steps: 4, tracks: [\n    { wave: 'pulse', vol: .15, notes: 'E5 - G5 - A5 - - C6 B5 - A5 - G5 - E5 - | D5 - E5 - G5 - - A5 G5 - E5 - D5 - . . | E5 - G5 - A5 - - C6 D6 - C6 - A5 - G5 - | A5 - G5 - E5 - D5 - C5 - - - - - . .' },","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium__20261102-184717__xe8b2f0/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019ycTDDGLRNkVgmJTnUg3XT","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
